        'Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: "When you hear the call to prayer, say what the caller says, then send blessings upon me, for whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him. Then ask Allah to grant me the wasilah, for it is a rank in Paradise that is fit for only one servant of Allah, and I hope that I am him. Whoever asks for the wasilah for me, my intercession becomes due for him." Narrated by Muslim.',
  ),
