  'dc309696da5': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The Prophet\'s way of drinking',
    text:
        'The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to drink in three breaths. When he brought the vessel to his mouth he mentioned the name of Allah (Bismillah), and when he took it away he praised Allah (Alhamdulillah). He did this three times.',
  ),
  'd67264100f2': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: '"And remember Allah during the appointed days"',
    reference: 'Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 203',
    text:
        'Allah the Almighty linked Hajj with dhikr and made it one of the most important aims of the fifth pillar of the religion. He the Almighty said: "And proclaim to the people the Hajj; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel, coming from every distant pass. That they may witness benefits for themselves and mention the name of Allah on known days over what He has provided them of [sacrificial] animals." [Al-Hajj 27-28] So He made it one of the most important aims of Hajj that the servant remembers Allah and thanks Him.\n\n'
        'The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) confirmed the link between Hajj and the remembrance of Allah when he said: "Circling the House, going between Safa and Marwa, and stoning the pillars were only made to establish the remembrance of Allah."\n\n'
        'This is how the place of dhikr in Hajj shows itself, and how great its status and high rank become clear. Below are the Prophetic supplications and dhikr reported for the stages of Hajj, its times and places, and for Umrah and the visit. Memorize them, so that your Hajj may be accepted and your effort appreciated.',
  ),
