  'd46799e66f0': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The meaning of dua',
    reference: 'Surah Ghafir, verse 60',
    text:
        'Dua is when the one who calls asks for what benefits them and what removes their harm. Its reality is showing one\'s need of Allah and renouncing all power and strength. It is the mark of servanthood and a feeling of human lowliness, and it carries the meaning of praising Allah the Almighty and attributing generosity and bounty to Him.\n\n'
        'Dua is obedience to Allah and compliance with His command. Allah the Almighty said: "And your Lord says: Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell, humbled."\n\n'
        'Dua is worship. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Dua is worship."\n\n'
        'Dua is the most honoured thing to Allah the Almighty. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Nothing is more honoured to Allah the Almighty than dua."\n\n'
        'Dua keeps away Allah\'s anger. He said: "Whoever does not ask Allah, He becomes angry with him."\n\n'
        'Dua protects from helplessness and shows good sense. He said: "The most helpless of people is the one who is helpless in making dua, and the stingiest of people is the one who is stingy with the greeting of peace."\n\n'
        'Dua lifts affliction. He said: "Whoever has the door of dua opened for him, the doors of mercy are opened for him, and Allah is never asked for anything He loves more than being asked for well-being." And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Dua benefits against what has descended and what has not yet descended, so hold fast to dua, servants of Allah."\n\n'
        'The one who makes dua is with Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Allah the Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."\n\n'
        'The virtue of dua in prostration. He said: "The closest a servant is to his Lord the Almighty is when he is prostrating, so make plenty of dua."\n\n'
        'The virtue of dua at night. He said: "In the night there is an hour in which no Muslim man asks Allah the Almighty for anything of this world and the next except that He gives it to him, and that is every night."\n\n'
        'The virtue of making dua for Muslims in their absence. He said: "There is no Muslim servant who makes dua for his brother in his absence except that the angel says: And for you the same."',
  ),
  'dea10b0e3a1': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle:
        'Verses and hadiths on the virtue of dhikr and dua, and the encouragement to do them',
    text:
        'Among the best of the easy righteous deeds that bring a Muslim closer to their Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, is dhikr. Many verses and authentic hadiths from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) have been reported about the virtue of dhikr and dua and the encouragement to do them. We mention some of them.\n\n'
        'Allah the Almighty said: "And the remembrance of Allah is greater." And He said: "And glorify Him morning and evening." And He said: "So remember Me; I will remember you. And be grateful to Me and do not deny Me." And He said: "O you who believe, remember Allah with much remembrance." And He said: "And the men who remember Allah often and the women who do so, Allah has prepared for them forgiveness and a great reward." And He said: "And remember your Lord much and glorify Him in the evening and the morning." And He said: "Those who remember Allah standing and sitting and on their sides." And He said: "And when you have completed your rites, remember Allah as you remember your fathers, or with greater remembrance." And He said: "O you who believe, let not your wealth and your children distract you from the remembrance of Allah." And He said: "And remember your Lord within yourself in humility and fear, and without loud speech, in the mornings and the evenings, and do not be among the heedless."\n\n'
        'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "The example of the one who remembers his Lord and the one who does not is like that of the living and the dead."\n\n'
        'He said: "Shall I not tell you of the best of your deeds, the purest in the sight of your King, the highest in your ranks, and better for you than spending gold and silver, and better for you than meeting your enemy and striking their necks while they strike yours?" They said: "Yes." He said: "The remembrance of Allah the Almighty."\n\n'
        'He said: "Allah the Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself. If he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than theirs. If he draws near to Me by a hand\'s span, I draw near to him by an arm\'s length. If he draws near to Me by an arm\'s length, I draw near to him by a fathom. And if he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."\n\n'
        'He said: "Whoever sits in a place in which he does not remember Allah, it will be a loss for him from Allah, and whoever lies down in a place in which he does not remember Allah, it will be a loss for him."\n\n'
        'He said: "No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah and do not send blessings upon their Prophet, but it will be a loss for them. If He wills He punishes them, and if He wills He forgives them."\n\n'
        'He said: "No people rise from a gathering in which they did not remember Allah except that they rise from the like of the carcass of a donkey, and it will be a regret for them."\n\n'
        'The virtues of dhikr, according to Imam Ibn al-Qayyim al-Jawziyyah\n\n'
        'It drives away the devil, subdues him and breaks him.\n\n'
        'It pleases the Most Merciful, the Mighty and Majestic.\n\n'
        'It removes worry and grief from the heart.\n\n'
        'It brings the heart joy, happiness and ease.\n\n'
        'It brings provision.\n\n'
        'It clothes the one who remembers with dignity, sweetness and radiance.\n\n'
        'It brings them love, which is the soul of Islam, the pivot of the religion and the axis of happiness and salvation. Allah has made a cause for everything, and He made the cause of love constant dhikr. So whoever wants to gain the love of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, let him keep His remembrance on his tongue, for it is the study and the revision, just as it is the door of knowledge. Dhikr is the door of love, its great highway and its straight path.\n\n'
        'It brings them watchfulness, until it admits them to the door of excellence (ihsan), so that they worship Allah as if they see Him. There is no way for the one who is heedless of dhikr to the station of ihsan, just as there is no way for someone sitting down to reach the House.\n\n'
        'It brings them turning back to Allah (inabah), which is returning to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. The more they return to Him through His remembrance, the more their heart returns to Him in all their states, so that Allah remains their refuge, their shelter, their haven, their protection, the direction of their heart and the place they flee to in calamities and trials.\n\n'
        'It brings them awe of their Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, and reverence for Him, because He takes hold of their heart and they are present with Allah the Almighty, unlike the heedless, whose veil of awe is thin.\n\n'
        'It brings them Allah\'s remembrance of them, as He the Almighty said: "So remember Me; I will remember you." If dhikr had only this, it would be enough as a virtue and an honour. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, narrating from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted: "Whoever remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself, and whoever remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than theirs." Narrated by Al-Bukhari and Muslim.\n\n'
        'It wipes away sins and removes them, for it is among the greatest good deeds, and good deeds erase bad deeds.\n\n'
        'It removes the estrangement between the servant and his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, for the heedless person has an estrangement between him and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that does not go away except through dhikr.\n\n'
        'When the servant gets to know Allah the Almighty through remembering Him in times of ease, Allah knows him in times of hardship. A report with this meaning has come, that when an obedient servant who remembers Allah the Almighty is struck by hardship or asks Allah the Almighty for a need, the angels say: "O Lord, a familiar voice from a familiar servant." And when the heedless one who turns away from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, calls on Him and asks Him, the angels say: "O Lord, an unfamiliar voice from an unfamiliar servant." And the hadith of Ibn Abbas: "Get to know Allah in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship." Narrated by Imam Ahmad.\n\n'
        'It saves from the punishment of Allah the Almighty, as Mu\'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said, and it is reported as a saying of the Prophet: "No son of Adam did a deed that saves more from the punishment of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, than the remembrance of Allah the Almighty." Narrated by Ahmad, Malik, Ibn Majah and At-Tirmidhi.\n\n'
        'It is a cause for tranquility to descend, for mercy to cover them, and for the angels to surround the one who remembers, as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told: "No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him." Narrated by Muslim.\n\n'
        'It keeps the tongue busy and away from backbiting, gossip, lying, obscenity and falsehood. A servant must speak. If he does not speak with the remembrance of Allah the Almighty and the mention of His commands, he will speak with these forbidden things or some of them, and there is no way to be safe from them at all except through the remembrance of Allah the Almighty. Observation and experience both bear witness to this. Whoever accustoms his tongue to the remembrance of Allah protects his tongue from falsehood and idle talk, and whoever lets his tongue go dry of the remembrance of Allah the Almighty, it becomes moist with every falsehood, idle talk and obscenity. There is no power and no strength except with Allah.\n\n'
        'It makes the servant safe from regret on the Day of Resurrection, for every gathering in which the servant does not remember his Lord, the Almighty, will be a regret and a loss for him on the Day of Resurrection.\n\n'
        'It is the easiest of acts of worship, and among the most majestic and best of them, for moving the tongue is the lightest and easiest movement of the limbs. If any other part of a person moved as much as the tongue does in a day and a night, it would be extremely hard for them, indeed impossible. In the hadith: "Two words, light on the tongue, heavy on the scale, beloved to the Most Merciful: Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi, Subhan Allahil-\'Azim."\n\n'
        'It is the planting of Paradise. In At-Tirmidhi, in the hadith of Abu az-Zubayr from Jabir, the Prophet said: "Whoever says Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi, a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise." At-Tirmidhi said: a good, sound hadith. Al-Albani graded it sound in Sahih al-Jami\' 6429.\n\n'
        'The gift and bounty attached to it are not attached to any other deed. In the two Sahihs, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah said: "Whoever says La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa \'ala kulli shay\'in qadir, a hundred times in a day, it is equal to freeing ten slaves, a hundred good deeds are written for him, a hundred bad deeds are erased from him, and it is a protection for him from the devil that day until evening. No one brings anything better than what he brings, except a man who did more than that. And whoever says Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi a hundred times in a day, his sins are wiped away even if they are like the foam of the sea." And in Sahih Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah said: "To say Subhan Allah, walhamdulillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu akbar is more beloved to me than everything the sun rises upon."\n\n'
        'Constant remembrance of the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, brings safety from forgetting Him, which is a cause of the servant\'s misery in his life and in the hereafter. For forgetting the Lord, Glory be to Him, leads to forgetting oneself and one\'s own good. The Almighty said: "And be not like those who forgot Allah, so He made them forget themselves. Those are the defiantly disobedient." When a servant forgets himself, he turns away from his own good, forgets it and busies himself with something else, and he is certainly ruined and corrupted. So whoever forgets Allah the Almighty, Allah makes him forget himself in this world and forgets him in the punishment on the Day of Resurrection. The Almighty said: "And whoever turns away from My remembrance, indeed, he will have a depressed life, and We will gather him on the Day of Resurrection blind. He will say: My Lord, why have you raised me blind while I used to see? He will say: Thus did Our signs come to you, and you forgot them; and thus today you will be forgotten." That is, forgotten in the punishment, as you forgot My signs and did not remember them or act upon them.\n\n'
        'Dhikr is a light for the one who remembers, in this world, in their grave and in their return. It goes ahead of them on the Bridge. Nothing lights up the hearts and the graves like the remembrance of Allah the Almighty. Allah the Almighty said: "Is one who was dead and We gave him life and made for him a light by which he walks among the people like one who is in darknesses from which he cannot come out?" The first is the believer, enlightened by faith in Allah, love for Him, knowledge of Him and remembrance of Him. The other is the one who is heedless of Allah the Almighty, who turns away from His remembrance and love. The whole matter and all success lie in light, and all misery lies in missing it.\n\n'
        'Dhikr gathers what is scattered, scatters what is gathered, brings near what is far and takes far what is near.\n\n'
        'There is a hardness in the heart that only the remembrance of Allah the Almighty can melt, so a servant should treat the hardness of his heart with the remembrance of Allah. Hammad ibn Zayd mentioned from Al-Mu\'alla ibn Ziyad that a man said to Al-Hasan: "O Abu Sa\'id, I complain to you of the hardness of my heart." He said: "Melt it with dhikr." This is because the more heedlessness grows in the heart, the more its hardness grows, and when Allah the Almighty is remembered that hardness melts, as lead melts in fire. So hardness of hearts is melted by nothing like the remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.\n\n'
        'Dhikr brings the blessings of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and of His angels upon the one who remembers. Whoever Allah the Almighty and His angels send blessings upon has fully succeeded and fully triumphed. He the Almighty said: "O you who believe, remember Allah with much remembrance, and glorify Him morning and evening. It is He who sends blessings upon you, and His angels too, to bring you out from darknesses into the light, and He is ever Merciful to the believers."\n\n'
        'Gatherings of dhikr are the gatherings of the angels. Among the gatherings of this world, they have no gathering except one in which Allah the Almighty is remembered. As the two Sahihs report, from the hadith of Al-A\'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah said: "Allah has roaming angels, besides the recording angels, who go about the roads looking for the people of dhikr. When they find people remembering Allah the Almighty, they call to one another: Come to what you need. He said: They surround them with their wings up to the lowest heaven. Then their Lord the Almighty asks them, though He knows best about them: What are My servants saying? They say: They glorify You, magnify You and praise You. He says: Have they seen Me? They say: No, by Allah, they have not seen You. He says: How would it be if they had seen Me? They say: If they had seen You, they would be more intense in worshipping You, more intense in praising and glorifying You, and would glorify You more. He says: What do they ask for? They say: They ask You for Paradise. He says: Have they seen it? They say: No, by Allah, O Lord, they have not seen it. He says: How would it be if they had seen it? They say: If they had seen it, they would be more eager for it, would seek it more, and would desire it more. He says: What do they seek refuge from? They say: From the Fire. He says: Have they seen it? They say: No, by Allah, O Lord, they have not seen it. He says: How would it be if they had seen it? They say: If they had seen it, they would flee from it more and fear it more. He says: I make you witness that I have forgiven them. One of the angels says: Among them is so-and-so, who is not one of them, but came for some need. He says: They are the sitters, and the one who sits with them is not left wretched." This is from their blessing on themselves and on those who sit with them, and they have a share of His words: "And He has made me blessed wherever I am." So the believer is blessed wherever he settles, and the wicked is ill-omened wherever he settles. The gatherings of dhikr are the gatherings of the angels, and the gatherings of heedlessness are the gatherings of the devils. Each is attached to its like and its kind, and a person ends up with what suits them.\n\n'
        'Allah the Almighty boasts about those who remember Him before His angels, as Muslim reported in his Sahih from Abu Sa\'id al-Khudri, who said: Mu\'awiyah went out to a circle in the mosque and said: "What makes you sit here?" They said: "We sat to remember Allah the Almighty." He said: "By Allah, only that makes you sit?" They said: "By Allah, nothing makes us sit except that." He said: "I did not ask you to swear because I suspect you, and no one of my standing with the Messenger of Allah has narrated fewer hadiths from him than I have. The Messenger of Allah went out to a circle of his companions and said: What makes you sit here? They said: We sat to remember Allah the Almighty and to praise Him for guiding us to Islam and for favouring us with you. He said: By Allah, only that makes you sit? They said: By Allah, nothing makes us sit except that. He said: I did not ask you to swear because I suspect you, but Jibril came to me and told me that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, boasts about you before the angels." This boasting from the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is proof of the honour of dhikr with Him and of His love for it, and that it has a distinction over other deeds.\n\n'
        'All acts of worship were only prescribed to establish the remembrance of Allah the Almighty, and the aim of them is to attain that remembrance. He the Almighty said: "Establish prayer for My remembrance."\n\n'
        'The remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, makes the hard easy, makes the difficult simple and lightens burdens. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is not remembered over anything hard but it becomes easy, nor over anything difficult but it becomes simple, nor over any burden but it becomes light, nor any hardship but it lifts, nor any distress but it clears. The remembrance of Allah the Almighty is the relief after hardship, the ease after difficulty, and the relief after worry and grief.\n\n'
        'Much remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is a safeguard against hypocrisy, for the hypocrites remember Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, only a little. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said of the hypocrites: "and they do not remember Allah except a little." Ka\'b said: "Whoever remembers Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, often is free of hypocrisy." And for this reason, and Allah knows best, Allah the Almighty ended Surat Al-Munafiqun with His words: "O you who believe, let not your wealth and your children distract you from the remembrance of Allah. And whoever does that, those are the losers." In this is a warning against the trial of the hypocrites, who were heedless of the remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and so fell into hypocrisy.',
  ),
  'd00e32b30dc': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Fatiha',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Fatiha\n\n'
        'From Abu Sa\'id ibn al-Mu\'alla (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: "Shall I not teach you the greatest surah in the Quran before you leave the mosque?" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to leave the mosque, and I reminded him. He said: ""Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds." It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the Great Quran that I was given." Narrated by Al-Bukhari (6/4474) and Ahmad (24/15730).\n\n'
        'From Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: While Jibril was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he heard a creaking sound above him. He raised his head and said: "This is a door of heaven that has been opened today and was never opened before today." An angel came down from it, and Jibril said: "This is an angel who has come down to earth and never came down before today." He gave greetings and said: "Receive the good news of two lights that you have been given and that no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book (Al-Fatiha) and the last verses of Surat Al-Baqarah. You will not recite a single letter of them except that you will be given what it asks for." Narrated by Muslim (1/806) and An-Nasa\'i (2/912).\n\n'
        'From Ubayy ibn Ka\'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Allah has not revealed in the Torah or the Gospel anything like the Mother of the Quran, and it is the seven oft-repeated verses." Allah said: "It is divided between Me and My servant, and My servant will have what he asks for." Narrated by At-Tirmidhi (5/3125), who graded it sound, and An-Nasa\'i (2/914).\n\n'
        'From Abu Sa\'id al-Khudri, who said: We were on a journey and stopped, and a girl came and said: "The chief of the tribe has been stung, and our men are away. Is there anyone among you who can perform ruqyah?" A man whom we did not know to practise ruqyah stood up with her and recited ruqyah over him, and he recovered. The chief ordered thirty sheep for the man and gave us milk to drink. When the man came back, we asked him: "Were you good at ruqyah, or did you practise it?" He said: "I only recited the Mother of the Book." We said: "Do nothing until we come to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and ask him." When we reached Medina we mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: "How did he know it was a ruqyah? Divide the sheep and give me a share with you."\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Fatiha\n\n'
        'Very important: the weak hadiths are placed here so that they are not acted upon, and so that people know they are weak.\n\n'
        '"The Opening of the Book suffices as nothing else of the Quran suffices. If the Opening of the Book were placed in one pan of the scale and the Quran in the other, the Opening of the Book would outweigh the Quran seven times." [Very weak / Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 3996].\n\n'
        '"The Opening of the Book is a cure from poison." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 3997].\n\n'
        '"If you lay your side on the bed and recite the Opening of the Book and "Say: He is Allah, One", you are safe from everything except death." [Weak / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 347].\n\n'
        '"No servant recites the Opening of the Book and Ayat al-Kursi in a house, but that day the evil eye of humans and jinn will not touch them." [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3952].\n\n'
        '"The Opening of the Book is a cure for every disease." [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3951].\n\n'
        '"The Opening of the Book equals two thirds of the Quran." [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3949].',
  ),
  'dc7f9c42f35': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Baqarah',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Baqarah\n\n'
        'From Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: "Recite Surat Al-Baqarah, for taking it up is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot withstand it." Narrated by Muslim (1/804) and Ahmad in the Musnad (36/22146).\n\n'
        'From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "The devil flees from the house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited." Narrated by Muslim (1/780) and At-Tirmidhi (5/2877).\n\n'
        'From Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Do not make your houses graves. The devil flees from the house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited." Narrated by Muslim (780).\n\n'
        'From An-Nu\'man ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Allah wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and sent down two verses from it with which He sealed Surat Al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights without the devil coming near it." Ahmad (4/274, no. 18438) and At-Tirmidhi (5/159, no. 2882).\n\n'
        'From Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: "Recite the two radiant ones, Al-Baqarah and Aal Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds, pleading for those who recited them." Narrated by Muslim (1/840) and Ahmad in the Musnad (36/22193).\n\n'
        'The virtue of Ayat al-Kursi\n\n'
        'From Ubayy ibn Ka\'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "O Abu al-Mundhir, do you know which verse of the Book of Allah that you have is the greatest?" I said: "Allah and His Messenger know best." He said: "O Abu al-Mundhir, do you know which verse of the Book of Allah that you have is the greatest?" I said: ""Allah, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer" [Al-Baqarah: 255]." He struck me on the chest and said: "By Allah, may knowledge be easy for you, Abu al-Mundhir." Narrated by Muslim (1/810) and Abu Dawud (2/1460).\n\n'
        'From Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after every obligatory prayer, nothing stands between him and entering Paradise except death." Narrated by An-Nasa\'i in As-Sunan al-Kubra (9/9848) and At-Tabarani in Al-Mu\'jam al-Kabir (8/7523).\n\n'
        'The virtue of the last two verses of Surat Al-Baqarah\n\n'
        'From Abu Mas\'ud al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Whoever recites the two verses at the end of Surat Al-Baqarah in a night, they are enough for him." Narrated by Al-Bukhari (6/5008, 5009) and Muslim (1/808).\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Baqarah\n\n'
        '"Two verses are Quran, and they intercede, and they are among what Allah loves: the two verses at the end of Surat Al-Baqarah." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 154].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites Surat Al-Baqarah will be crowned with a crown in Paradise." (Fabricated) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 4633].\n\n'
        '"Everything has a peak, and the peak of the Quran is Surat Al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it in his house at night, the devil will not enter it for three nights, and whoever recites it in his house by day, the devil will not enter it for three days."',
  ),
  'd07d1864fd8': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Aal Imran',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Aal Imran\n\n'
        'From Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: "Recite the two radiant ones, Al-Baqarah and Aal Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds, pleading for those who recited them." Narrated by Muslim (1/840) and Ahmad in the Musnad (36/22193).\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Aal Imran\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites the surah in which Aal Imran is mentioned on Friday, Allah and His angels send blessings upon him until the sun sets." (Fabricated) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 415].\n\n'
        '"The Greatest Name of Allah, by which, if He is called upon, He answers, is in this verse of Aal Imran: "Say: O Allah, Owner of sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will", to its end." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 2772].\n\n'
        '"Shirk is more hidden in my community than the creeping of an ant on a rock on a dark night, and its lowest degree is to love something of injustice or to hate something of justice. And is religion anything but love for the sake of Allah and hatred for the sake of Allah? Allah the Almighty said: "Say: If you love Allah, then follow me, and Allah will love you" (Aal Imran: 31)." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 3755].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites the end of Aal Imran in a night, the standing of a night is written for him." [Da\'if Mishkat al-Masabih 2112].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites Surat Aal Imran on Friday, the angels send blessings upon him until night." [Da\'if Mishkat al-Masabih 2113].\n\n'
        '"There is no man on a difficult mount who says in its ear: "Do they seek other than the religion of Allah, while to Him submit all those in the heavens and earth, willingly or unwillingly, and to Him they will be returned" (Aal Imran: 83), except that it stops by Allah\'s permission." [Da\'if al-Kalim at-Tayyib 177].\n\n'
        '"Allah does not disappoint a servant who stands in the depth of the night and opens with Surat Al-Baqarah and Aal Imran. What a fine treasure for a person Al-Baqarah and Aal Imran are." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 5063].',
  ),
  'd795e16c760': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Kahf',
    text: 'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Kahf\n\n'
        'From Abu ad-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: "Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Al-Kahf is protected from the trial of the Dajjal." Narrated by Muslim (1/809), Abu Dawud (4/4323) and At-Tirmidhi (5/2886).\n\n'
        'From Abu Sa\'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet said: Whoever recites Surat Al-Kahf on Friday, a light will shine for him between the two Fridays. [Graded sound by Al-Albani in Sahih at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 736].\n\n'
        'From Abu Sa\'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet said: Whoever recites Surat Al-Kahf on the night of Friday, a light will shine for him between him and the Ancient House (the Kaaba). [Graded sound by Al-Albani in Sahih at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 736].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Kahf\n\n'
        '"Shall I not tell you of a surah whose greatness fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and whoever recites it has a reward like that? Whoever recites it is forgiven what is between him and the other Friday, and three days more." They said: "Yes." He said: "Surat Al-Kahf." [Very weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 2160].\n\n'
        '"Surat Al-Kahf is called in the Torah: the Barrier. It stands between its reciter and the Fire." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 3259].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites three verses from the beginning of Al-Kahf is protected from the trial of the Dajjal." [Da\'if Mishkat al-Masabih 2088].',
  ),
  'd8c2fc1280f': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Mulk',
    text: 'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Mulk\n\n'
        'From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: "There is a surah of the Quran, thirty verses, that intercedes for its companion until he is forgiven: "Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion"." Narrated by Abu Dawud (2/1400) and At-Tirmidhi (5/2891), who said: "A good hadith."\n\n'
        'From Jabir, who said: "The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would not sleep until he had recited Alif Lam Mim Tanzil (As-Sajdah) and Tabarak alladhi bi-yadihi al-mulk (Al-Mulk)." [Narrated by At-Tirmidhi and graded sound by Al-Albani, 2316].',
  ),
  'd6f2e399f63': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Kafirun',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Kafirun\n\n'
        'From Nawfal al-Ashja\'i (may Allah be pleased with him), that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: "O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to say when I go to my bed." He said: "Recite: "Say: O disbelievers", for it is a freedom from shirk." Narrated by Abu Dawud (4/5055) and At-Tirmidhi (5/3403), who graded it sound.',
  ),
  'd1dcf57234b': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Ikhlas',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Ikhlas\n\n'
        'From Abdullah ibn Mas\'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Quran every night?" They said: "Who can do that?" He said: "Indeed: "Say: He is Allah, One"." Narrated by Al-Bukhari (6/5015), Muslim (1/811) and Ahmad (14/11053).\n\n'
        'From Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: "I love this surah: "Say: He is Allah, One"." The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Your love for it will admit you to Paradise." Narrated by Al-Bukhari (1/p. 155) as a suspended report, and At-Tirmidhi (5/2901), who graded it good.\n\n'
        'From Mu\'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: "Whoever recites "Say: He is Allah, One" until he finishes it, ten times, Allah builds a palace for him in Paradise." Umar ibn al-Khattab said: "Then we will have many, O Messenger of Allah." The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Allah has more, and better." Narrated by Ahmad (15057), and graded sound by Al-Albani in Sahih al-Jami\' (6472).\n\n'
        'From Mu\'adh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father, who said: We went out on a rainy night of deep darkness looking for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to lead us in prayer. I found him, and he said: "Say." I did not say anything. Then he said: "Say." I did not say anything. He said: "Say." I said: "What shall I say?" He said: "Say: "Say: He is Allah, One" and the two Mu\'awwidhat, three times in the evening and the morning, and they will suffice you against everything." [Narrated by At-Tirmidhi and graded sound by Al-Albani, 2829].\n\n'
        'From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and he heard a man reciting "Say: He is Allah, One. Allah, the Eternal Refuge." The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "It is due." I said: "What is due?" He said: "Paradise." [Narrated by At-Tirmidhi and graded sound by Al-Albani, 2320].\n\n'
        'From Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and he said to me: "O Uqbah ibn Amir, shall I not teach you surahs the like of which were not revealed in the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel or the Furqan? Let no night come upon you without you reciting them in it: "Say: He is Allah, One", "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind"." Uqbah said: "No night has come upon me without my reciting them in it, and it is right that I never leave them, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me to recite them." [Silsilat al-Ahadith as-Sahihah 2861]\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Ikhlas\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites "Say: He is Allah, One" in the illness in which he dies will not be tried in his grave, will be safe from the squeezing of the grave, and on the Day of Resurrection the angels will carry him on their palms until they take him across the Bridge into Paradise." (Fabricated) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 301].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites "Say: He is Allah, One" twenty times, Allah builds a palace for him in Paradise." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 1351].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites "Say: He is Allah, One" two hundred times, the sins of two hundred years are forgiven him." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 295].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites "Say: He is Allah, One" two hundred times, Allah writes for him one thousand five hundred good deeds, unless he has a debt." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 300].\n\n'
        '"Whoever passes by the graves and recites "Say: He is Allah, One" eleven times, then gives its reward to the dead, will be given a reward as many as the dead." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 1290].\n\n'
        '"Whoever prays the morning prayer, then recites "Say: He is Allah, One" a hundred times before speaking, each time he recites it a sin of a year is forgiven him." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 405].\n\n'
        '"Whoever passes by the graves and recites in them eleven times: "Say: He is Allah, One", then gives its reward to the dead, will be given a reward as many as the dead." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 3277].\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites after the Friday prayer "Say: He is Allah, One", "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind" seven times, Allah protects him by them from evil until the next Friday." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 4129].',
  ),
  'dcffadeb774': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Falaq and An-Nas (the two Mu\'awwidhat)',
    text:
        'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Falaq and An-Nas (the two Mu\'awwidhat)\n\n'
        'From Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Have you not seen verses revealed tonight the like of which has never been seen: "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind"?" Narrated by Muslim (1/814) and Abu Dawud (2/1462).\n\n'
        'From Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: "Recite, O Jabir." I said: "What shall I recite, may my father and mother be your ransom?" He said: "Recite: "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind"." So I recited them, and he said: "Recite them, for you will never recite anything like them." Narrated by An-Nasa\'i (8/5441) and Ibn Hibban (3/796). It is a good hadith.\n\n'
        'From Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and he said to me: "O Uqbah ibn Amir, shall I not teach you surahs the like of which were not revealed in the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel or the Furqan? Let no night come upon you without you reciting them in it: "Say: He is Allah, One", "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind"." Uqbah said: "No night has come upon me without my reciting them in it, and it is right that I never leave them, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me to recite them." [Silsilat al-Ahadith as-Sahihah 2861]\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Falaq and An-Nas (the two Mu\'awwidhat)\n\n'
        '"Whoever recites after the Friday prayer "Say: He is Allah, One", "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak" and "Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind" seven times, Allah protects him by them from evil until the next Friday." [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 4129].',
  ),
  'd22d7d455ac': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Hud',
    text: 'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Hud\n\n'
        'From Ibn Abbas, who said: Abu Bakr said: "O Messenger of Allah, you have gone grey." He said: "Hud, Al-Waqi\'ah, Al-Mursalat, An-Naba and At-Takwir have turned me grey." [Narrated by At-Tirmidhi and graded sound by Al-Albani in Sahih al-Jami\' 3723].\n\n'
        'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Hud and its sisters have turned me grey before my time." [Sahih al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3721].\n\n'
        'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Hud and its sisters from the Mufassal have turned me grey." [Sahih al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3722].\n\n'
        'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Hud and its sisters have turned me grey." [Sahih ash-Shama\'il al-Muhammadiyyah 35].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Hud\n\n'
        '"Hud and its sisters, and what was done to the nations before me, have turned me grey." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3421].\n\n'
        '"Recite Surat Hud on Friday." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 1070].\n\n'
        '"Hud and its sisters, Al-Waqi\'ah, Al-Haqqah and At-Takwir, have turned me grey." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3419].\n\n'
        '"Surat Hud and its sisters, Al-Waqi\'ah, Al-Qari\'ah, Al-Haqqah, At-Takwir and Sa\'ala sa\'il, have turned me grey." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3418].\n\n'
        '"Hud and its sisters, the mention of the Day of Resurrection and the stories of the nations, have turned me grey." [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3420].',
  ),
  'dfb28ac7ad9': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Isra',
    text: 'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Isra\n\n'
        'From Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: "The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would not sleep until he had recited Az-Zumar and Bani Isra\'il (Al-Isra)." [Silsilat al-Ahadith as-Sahihah 641].\n\n'
        'From Al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) "would not sleep until he had recited the Musabbihat, and he would say: In them is a verse better than a thousand verses." [Narrated by At-Tirmidhi and graded sound by Al-Albani, 2712].\n\n'
        'The Musabbihat are the surahs that begin with "Sabbaha" or "Yusabbihu" (glorified): Al-Isra, Al-Hadid, Al-Hashr, As-Saff, Al-Jumu\'ah, At-Taghabun and Al-A\'la.',
  ),
  'd0fd90b8251': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtue of Surah Al-Fath',
    text: 'The authentic hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Fath\n\n'
        'From Anas, that it was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on his way back from Al-Hudaybiyah, while his companions were mixed with grief and sadness, for they had been kept from their homes and had slaughtered the sacrificial animals at Al-Hudaybiyah ("Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest" up to His words "a straight path"). He said: "Two verses have been revealed to me that are dearer to me than the whole world." [Narrated by Ahmad and graded sound by Al-Albani in Sahih al-Jami\' 5121].',
  ),
  'd3ab8fecf88': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'Weak hadiths reported about the virtues of some surahs',
    text:
        'Very important: the weak hadiths are placed here so that they are not acted upon, and so that people know they are weak.\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Ya-Sin\n\n'
        'All the narrations reported about the virtue of Surat Ya-Sin are weak or fabricated.\n\n'
        '(Allah, Blessed and Exalted, recited Ta-Ha and Ya-Sin two thousand years before He created Adam. When the angels heard the Quran they said: Blessed is the nation upon whom this is sent down, and blessed are the tongues that speak this, and blessed are the hearts that carry this.) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 1248].\n\n'
        '(Whoever enters the graveyard and recites Surat Ya-Sin, it is lightened for them that day, and he has good deeds as many as those in it.) [Fabricated / Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 1246].\n\n'
        '(Everything has a heart, and the heart of the Quran is Ya-Sin. Whoever recites Ya-Sin, Allah writes for him by that recitation the reward of reciting the Quran ten times.) [Fabricated / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 885].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Ya-Sin seeking the face of Allah, Allah forgives him what came before of his sins, so recite it over your dying.) (Weak) [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 5785].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Ya-Sin at the beginning of the day, his needs are met.) [Weak / Da\'if Mishkat al-Masabih 2118].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Ad-Dukhan\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Surat Ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday is forgiven.) [Very weak. Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 4632].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Surat Ad-Dukhan in a night, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him until morning.) [Fabricated / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 978].\n\n'
        '(Whoever prays with Surat Ad-Dukhan in a night, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him through the night.) [Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 448].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Ha-Mim Ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday or on Friday, Allah builds a house for him in Paradise.) [Very weak / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 449].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Surat Ya-Sin in a night wakes up forgiven. Whoever recites Ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday wakes up forgiven.) [Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 978].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Ghafir\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites all of Ad-Dukhan, and the beginning of Ha-Mim Ghafir up to "and to Him is the final destination", and Ayat al-Kursi in the evening is protected by them until morning, and whoever recites them in the morning is protected by them until evening.) [Weak / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 390].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Hashr\n\n'
        '(Whoever says three times in the morning: "A\'udhu billahis-sami\'il-\'alimi minash-shaytanir-rajim" (I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed devil), and recites three verses from the end of Surat Al-Hashr, Allah appoints seventy thousand angels over him to send blessings upon him until evening, and if he dies that day he dies a martyr, and whoever says it in the evening has the same rank.) [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 5732].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites the last verses of Al-Hashr by night or by day and dies that day or night, Paradise is assured for him.) [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 5770].\n\n'
        '(The Greatest Name of Allah is in the six verses at the end of Surat Al-Hashr.) [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 853].\n\n'
        '(When you lie down on your side, recite Surat Al-Hashr; if you die, you die a martyr.) [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 307].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Ar-Rahman\n\n'
        '(Everything has a bride, and the bride of the Quran is Ar-Rahman.) [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 4729].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Waqi\'ah\n\n'
        '(Teach your women Surat Al-Waqi\'ah, for it is the surah of wealth.) [Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 3730].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Surat Al-Waqi\'ah and learns it will not be written among the heedless, and neither he nor his household will be poor.) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 291].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites Surat Al-Waqi\'ah every night will never be struck by poverty.) [Weak / Da\'if al-Jami\' as-Saghir 5773].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Az-Zalzalah\n\n'
        '("When the earth is shaken" equals half the Quran.) [Weak / Da\'if at-Targhib wa-t-Tarhib 889].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Ash-Sharh and Surat Al-Fil\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites "Have We not expanded" and "Have you not seen how" in the Fajr prayer will not suffer from sore eyes.) [No basis / Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 67].\n\n'
        'Weak hadiths reported about the virtue of Surat Al-Qadr\n\n'
        '(Reciting Surat "Indeed, We sent it down" after wudu.) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 68].\n\n'
        '(Whoever recites right after his wudu "Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Power" once is among the truthful, whoever recites it twice is written in the register of the martyrs, and whoever recites it three times, Allah gathers him with the prophets.) [Silsilat al-Ahadith ad-Da\'ifah 1449].',
  ),
  'd5296c02d24': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle: 'The virtues of the Noble Quran',
    text: 'The people of the Quran are the people of Allah.\n\n'
        'The reward of reciting the Quran is greater than the most precious wealth of this world.\n\n'
        'Every letter of it earns ten good deeds.\n\n'
        'It brings a person comfort and a good name in the heavens and on earth.\n\n'
        'For every verse a Muslim memorizes, Allah raises them one rank in Paradise.\n\n'
        'Whoever is skilled in the Quran is joined by Allah the Almighty with the noblest of the angels.\n\n'
        'The best of people is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it.\n\n'
        'Allah the Almighty does not punish a person who memorized the Quran and acted upon it.\n\n'
        'It comes as an intercessor for those who acted upon it in this world.\n\n'
        'The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised the companion of the Quran to the ranks of the scholars.\n\n'
        'Allah the Almighty honours the companion of the Quran, and their parents, on the Day of Resurrection with great kinds of honour.\n\n'
        'The Quran is among the greatest and most beloved means of drawing near to Allah.\n\n'
        'All people are written every night among the heedless, except whoever recites the Quran.\n\n'
        'The house in which the Quran is recited gains goodness and blessings, and Allah the Almighty protects its people from every harm.',
  ),
  'd862d5ef8a4': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle:
        'Verses that call for reciting the Quran, reflecting on it and being moved by it',
    text:
        'Allah the Almighty said: "And when the Quran is recited, then listen to it and pay attention, that you may receive mercy." [Al-A\'raf 204].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We send down of the Quran that which is healing and mercy for the believers, but it does not increase the wrongdoers except in loss." [Al-Isra 82].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Indeed, this Quran guides to that which is most suitable and gives good tidings to the believers who do righteous deeds that they will have a great reward." [Al-Isra 9]\n\n'
        'And He said: "[This is] a blessed Book which We have revealed to you, that they might reflect upon its verses and that those of understanding would be reminded." [Sad 29]\n\n'
        'And He said: "And recite the Quran with measured recitation." [Al-Muzzammil 4]\n\n'
        'And He said: "And if there was any Quran by which the mountains would be removed or the earth would be broken apart or the dead would be made to speak... Rather, to Allah belongs the affair entirely. Then have those who believe not accepted that had Allah willed, He could have guided the people all together? And those who disbelieve do not cease to be struck, because of what they have done, by calamity or have it descend near their home until there comes the promise of Allah. Indeed, Allah does not fail in the promise." [Ar-Ra\'d 31].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And the Messenger has said: O my Lord, indeed my people have taken this Quran as something abandoned." [Al-Furqan 30].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Then do they not reflect upon the Quran? If it had been from other than Allah, they would have found within it much contradiction." [An-Nisa 82].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Say: What thing is greatest as a witness? Say: Allah is witness between me and you. And this Quran has been revealed to me that I may warn you thereby and whomever it reaches. Do you actually bear witness that with Allah there are other deities? Say: I do not bear witness. Say: Indeed, He is but one God, and indeed, I am free of what you associate with Him." [Al-An\'am 19].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And it was not possible for this Quran to be produced by other than Allah, but it is a confirmation of what was before it and a detailed explanation of the Scripture, about which there is no doubt, from the Lord of the worlds." [Yunus 37].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have certainly given you seven of the often repeated verses and the great Quran." [Al-Hijr 87].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Who have made the Quran into portions." [Al-Hijr 91].\n\n'
        'And He said: "So when you recite the Quran, seek refuge in Allah from Satan, the expelled." [An-Nahl 98].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have certainly diversified the contents of this Quran that they may be reminded, but it does not increase them except in aversion." [Al-Isra 41].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have placed over their hearts coverings, lest they understand it, and in their ears deafness. And when you mention your Lord alone in the Quran, they turn back in aversion." [Al-Isra 46].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And when you recite the Quran, We put between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a concealed partition." [Al-Isra 45].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Say: If mankind and the jinn gathered in order to produce the like of this Quran, they could not produce the like of it, even if they were to each other assistants." [Al-Isra 88].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have certainly diversified in this Quran for the people from every kind of example; but man has ever been, most of anything, argumentative." [Al-Kahf 54].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Ta, Ha. We have not sent down to you the Quran that you be distressed. But only as a reminder for those who fear Allah. A revelation from He who created the earth and the highest heavens. The Most Merciful, who is above the Throne established." [Ta-Ha 1-5].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Indeed, this Quran relates to the Children of Israel most of that over which they disagree. And indeed, it is guidance and mercy for the believers." [An-Naml 76-77].\n\n'
        'And He said: "I have only been commanded to worship the Lord of this city, who made it sacred and to whom belongs all things. And I am commanded to be of the Muslims. And to recite the Quran. And whoever is guided is only guided for the benefit of his soul; and whoever strays, say: I am only one of the warners." [An-Naml 91-92].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have certainly presented for the people in this Quran from every example. But if you bring them a sign, those who disbelieve will surely say: You are not but falsifiers." [Ar-Rum 58].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Say: It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened and said: Indeed, we have heard an amazing Quran. It guides to the right course, and we have believed in it. And we will never associate with our Lord anyone." [Al-Jinn 1-2].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And those who disbelieve say: Do not listen to this Quran and speak noisily during it that perhaps you will overcome." [Fussilat 26].\n\n'
        'And He said: "The month of Ramadan is that in which was revealed the Quran, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion. So whoever sights the new moon of the month, let him fast it; and whoever is ill or on a journey, then an equal number of other days. Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship, and wants for you to complete the period and to glorify Allah for that to which He has guided you; and perhaps you will be grateful." [Al-Baqarah 185].\n\n'
        'And He said: "If We had sent down this Quran upon a mountain, you would have seen it humbled and coming apart from fear of Allah. And these examples We present to the people that perhaps they will give thought." [Al-Hashr 21].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Ha, Mim. By the clear Book, indeed, We sent it down during a blessed night. Indeed, We were to warn mankind." [Ad-Dukhan 1-3].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree. And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months. The angels and the Spirit descend therein by permission of their Lord for every matter. Peace it is until the emergence of dawn." [Al-Qadr 1-5].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And those who disbelieve say: Why was the Quran not revealed to him all at once? Thus it is, that We may strengthen thereby your heart. And We have spaced it distinctly." [Al-Furqan 32].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And when We directed to you a few of the jinn, listening to the Quran. When they attended it, they said: Listen quietly. And when it was concluded, they went back to their people as warners. They said: O our people, indeed we have heard a Book revealed after Moses confirming what was before it which guides to the truth and to a straight path." [Al-Ahqaf 29-30].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We have certainly made the Quran easy for remembrance, so is there any who will remember?" [Al-Qamar 17].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And this is a blessed message which We have sent down; so are you, of it, denying?" [Al-Anbiya 50].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And We did not give him knowledge of poetry, nor is it befitting for him. It is not but a reminder and a clear Quran. To warn whoever is alive and for the word to be justified against the disbelievers." [Ya-Sin 69-70].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Allah has sent down the best statement: a consistent Book wherein is reiteration. The skins of those who fear their Lord shiver therefrom; then their skins and their hearts relax at the remembrance of Allah. That is the guidance of Allah by which He guides whom He wills. And one whom Allah leaves astray, for him there is no guide." [Az-Zumar 23].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And this is a Book We have revealed, blessed, confirming what was before it, and that you may warn the Mother of Cities and those around it. And those who believe in the Hereafter believe in it, and they are maintaining their prayer." [Al-An\'am 92].\n\n'
        'And He said: "And those who disbelieve say: We will never believe in this Quran nor in that before it. But if you could see when the wrongdoers are made to stand before their Lord, refuting each other\'s words. Those who were oppressed will say to those who were arrogant: If not for you, we would have been believers." [Saba 31].\n\n'
        'And He said: "We have certainly sent down to you a Book in which is your mention. Then will you not reason?" [Al-Anbiya 10].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Alif, Lam, Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Quran that you might understand." [Yusuf 1-2].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Alif, Lam, Ra. A Book whose verses are perfected and then presented in detail from One who is Wise and Acquainted." [Hud 1].\n\n'
        'And He said: "Those to whom We have given the Book recite it as it should be recited. Those believe in it. And whoever disbelieves in it, it is they who are the losers." [Al-Baqarah 121].',
  ),
  'd70b27f03c9': DhikrEnglish(
    subtitle:
        'Hadiths that call for reciting the Quran, reflecting on it and being moved by it',
    text:
        'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: "Allah raises some people by this Book and lowers others by it."\n\n'
        'He said: "The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it."\n\n'
        'He said: "The believer who recites the Quran and acts upon it is like a citron: its taste is good and its smell is good. The believer who does not recite the Quran but acts upon it is like a date: its taste is good and it has no smell. The hypocrite who recites the Quran is like a basil plant: its smell is good and its taste is bitter. And the hypocrite who does not recite the Quran is like a colocynth: its taste is bitter, or foul, and its smell is bitter."\n\n'
        'He said: "The one who recites the Quran and has memorized it is with the noble, righteous angels (scribes). And the one who recites it, striving to keep it up while it is hard for him, has two rewards."\n\n'
        'He said: "The Book of Allah is the rope of Allah, stretched from heaven to earth."\n\n'
        'He said: "Whoever recites a letter from the Book of Allah has a good deed for it, and a good deed is multiplied by ten. I do not say that Alif-Lam-Mim is one letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter and Mim is a letter."\n\n'
        'He said: "Let me not find any of you reclining on his couch, when a matter of mine comes to him, of what I commanded or forbade, and he says: I do not know; we follow only what we find in the Book of Allah."\n\n'
        'He said: "There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah has given wealth and has enabled him to spend it in the right way, and a man whom Allah has given wisdom, who judges by it and teaches it."\n\n'
        'He said: "Allah commands you to have your community recite the Quran in seven modes, and whichever mode they recite it in, they are correct."\n\n'
        'He said: "The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to bring two of the men killed at Uhud together in one shroud, then say: Which of them took more of the Quran? When one of them was pointed out to him, he put him first in the grave and said: I will be a witness over these on the Day of Resurrection. He ordered them buried in their blood, without washing them or praying over them."\n\n'
        'He said: "Learn the Quran and ask Allah for Paradise by it, before a people learn it and ask this world by it. The Quran is learned by three: a man who boasts with it, a man who earns his living by it, and a man who recites it for Allah."\n\n'
        'He said: "He is not one of us who does not make his voice beautiful with the Quran."\n\n'
        'He said: "The one who has nothing of the Quran in him is like a ruined house."\n\n'
        'He said: "Allah has family among people." They said: "O Messenger of Allah, who are they?" He said: "They are the people of the Quran, the people of Allah and His chosen ones."\n\n'
        'He said: "It will be said to the companion of the Quran: Recite, and rise, and recite in slow measured tones as you used to recite in the world, for your rank is at the last verse you recite."\n\n'
        'He said: "The Quran will come on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Lord, adorn him. So he will be clothed with the crown of honour. Then it will say: O Lord, give him more. So he will be clothed with the garment of honour. Then it will say: O Lord, be pleased with him. So He will be pleased with him. And it will be said to him: Recite and rise, and for every verse you will be given a good deed."',
  ),
